<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head><meta charset="UTF-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0"><title><%= title %> - EliteHackLab</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/style.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/6.5.1/css/all.min.css"></head>
<body>
  <div class="matrix-bg"></div>
  <nav class="main-nav"><div class="nav-brand"><span class="brand-icon">💀</span><span class="brand-text">Elite<span class="highlight">Hack</span>Lab</span></div><div class="nav-links"><a href="/"><i class="fas fa-home"></i> Dashboard</a></div></nav>
  <div class="lab-container">
    <div class="lab-header"><h1><i class="fas fa-user-secret"></i> Man-in-the-Middle Attack</h1><div class="lab-info"><span class="lab-tag difficulty-hard">Hard</span></div></div>
    <div class="lab-section"><h2><i class="fas fa-crosshairs"></i> Objective</h2><p>Understand how MITM attacks work by analyzing the attack flow. Intercept the simulated communication between two parties and extract the secret message.</p></div>
    <div class="lab-section"><h2><i class="fas fa-project-diagram"></i> Attack Diagram</h2>
      <div class="code-block">
        <pre>
    Normal Communication:
    ┌──────────┐                           ┌──────────┐
    │  Alice   │ ─────── Secure ─────────▶ │   Bob    │
    │ (Client) │ ◀────── Channel ───────── │ (Server) │
    └──────────┘                           └──────────┘

    MITM Attack:
    ┌──────────┐         ┌──────────┐         ┌──────────┐
    │  Alice   │ ──────▶ │  Mallory │ ──────▶ │   Bob    │
    │ (Client) │ ◀────── │ (Attacker)│ ◀────── │ (Server) │
    └──────────┘         └──────────┘         └──────────┘
                          │
                          ▼ Reads/Modifies
                     ┌──────────┐
                     │ Captured │
                     │   Data   │
                     └──────────┘

    Attack Steps:
    1. ARP Spoofing → Redirect traffic through attacker
    2. SSL Stripping → Downgrade HTTPS to HTTP
    3. Traffic Capture → Read plaintext data
    4. Data Injection → Modify responses
        </pre>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="lab-section"><h2><i class="fas fa-terminal"></i> MITM Simulation</h2>
      <div class="vulnerable-form">
        <p>Simulate intercepting traffic between Alice (192.168.1.10) and Bob (192.168.1.20):</p>
        <button class="btn" onclick="startMitm()"><i class="fas fa-play"></i> Start MITM Attack</button>
        <button class="btn" onclick="captureTraffic()" style="margin-left:0.5rem;"><i class="fas fa-download"></i> Capture Traffic</button>
      </div>
      <div id="mitmResults" class="result-box" style="margin-top:1rem;"></div>
      <div class="code-block">
        <h4><i class="fas fa-lightbulb"></i> Hints</h4>
        <pre>
# MITM tools:
ettercap -T -M arp:remote /192.168.1.10// /192.168.1.20//
mitmproxy --mode transparent
bettercap -iface eth0

# Prevention:
- Use HTTPS with HSTS
- Certificate pinning
- VPN connections
- Network segmentation
        </pre>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="flag-submit"><h3><i class="fas fa-flag"></i> Capture The Flag</h3>
      <form onsubmit="submitFlagInline('network-mitm','flagInput_mitm','flagResult_mitm'); return false;" style="display:flex; gap:0.5rem; max-width:500px; margin:0 auto;"><input type="text" id="flagInput_mitm" placeholder="FLAG{...}" autocomplete="off"><button type="submit" class="btn">Submit</button></form>
      <div id="flagResult_mitm" style="display:none; margin-top:1rem;"></div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <script src="/js/main.js"></script>
  <script>
    async function startMitm() {
      const resultsDiv = document.getElementById('mitmResults');
      resultsDiv.innerHTML = '<p style="color:var(--primary)"><i class="fas fa-spinner fa-spin"></i> Enabling IP forwarding and ARP spoofing...</p>';
      try {
        const res = await fetch('/api/labs/network/mitm', { method: 'POST', headers: {'Content-Type':'application/json'}, body: JSON.stringify({ action: 'start' }) });
        const data = await res.json();
        resultsDiv.innerHTML = '<p style="color:#00ff00"><i class="fas fa-check"></i> ' + data.message + '</p>';
      } catch(e) { resultsDiv.innerHTML = '<p style="color:#ff4444">Error: ' + e.message + '</p>'; }
    }
    async function captureTraffic() {
      const resultsDiv = document.getElementById('mitmResults');
      resultsDiv.innerHTML = '<p style="color:var(--primary)"><i class="fas fa-spinner fa-spin"></i> Capturing traffic...</p>';
      try {
        const res = await fetch('/api/labs/network/mitm', { method: 'POST', headers: {'Content-Type':'application/json'}, body: JSON.stringify({ action: 'capture' }) });
        const data = await res.json();
        let html = '<h4 style="color:var(--primary)">Intercepted Traffic:</h4>';
        if (data.captured) {
          data.captured.forEach(function(pkt) { html += '<p style="font-family:monospace;margin:0.25rem 0;">' + pkt + '</p>'; });
        }
        resultsDiv.innerHTML = html;
      } catch(e) { resultsDiv.innerHTML = '<p style="color:#ff4444">Error: ' + e.message + '</p>'; }
    }
  </script>
</body>
</html>
